  "pli-tv-kd10:2.6.7": "<i lang='pi' translate='no'>Viññutaṁ pāpuṇi</i>, literally, “reached discernment”. Commenting on a similar context at <a href='https://suttacentral.net/pli-tv-kd20/en/brahmali#25.1.6'>Kd 20:25.1.6</a>, Sp 4.432 explains: <i lang='pi' translate='no'>Yāva so dārako viññutaṁ pāpuṇātīti yāva khādituṁ bhuñjituṁ nahāyituñca maṇḍituñca attano dhammatāya sakkotīti attho</i>, “<i lang='pi' translate='no'>Yāva so dārako viññutaṁ pāpuṇāti</i> means until he is able to eat, bathe, and groom himself.” ",
